 seekers, often involving them in illegal activities like money laundering. Authorities advise verifying recruiters, avoiding sharing sensitive personal details, and reporting suspicious ads to safeguard individuals and the wider community from financial crime.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/dubai-police-warn-against-fake-part-time-job-scams-why-easy-money-could-cost-you-everything/articleshow/124310479.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/dubai-police-warn-against-fake-part-time-job-scams-why-easy-money-could-cost-you-everything/articleshow/124310479.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-10-04T22:43:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124310672,imgsize-1098557.cms"/></item><item><title>Angelton shooting: Two children fatally shot; other two critically injured near Houston</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124310614.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/angelton-shooting-two-children-fatally-shot-other-two-critically-injured-near-houston/articleshow/124310614.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/angelton-shooting-two-children-fatally-shot-other-two-critically-injured-near-houston/articleshow/124310614.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-10-04T22:38:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124310625,imgsize-421778.cms"/></item><item><title>'Guess who Kash Patel sent to investigate Charlie Kirk's assassination': Candace Owens drops new bombshell</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124310229.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/guess-who-kash-patel-sent-to-investigate-charlie-kirks-assassination-candace-owens-drops-new-bombshell/articleshow/124310229.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/guess-who-kash-patel-sent-to-investigate-charlie-kirks-assassination-candace-owens-drops-new-bombshell/articleshow/124310229.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-10-04T22:02:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124310223,imgsize-19684.cms"/></item><item><title>UN nuclear disarmament meet: India reaffirms ‘no first use’ policy; urges credible minimum deterrence</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124308677.cms" /&gt;India reaffirmed its responsible nuclear conduct at a United Nations meeting. It reiterated its no first use policy. The UN Secretary-General warned of a new nuclear arms race. Pakistan called for verifiable disarmament. Other nations shared nuclear testing experiences. Calls for nuclear-weapon-free zones also emerged. Geopolitical tensions were also flagged.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/un-nuclear-disarmament-meet-india-reaffirms-no-first-use-policy-urges-credible-minimum-deterrence/articleshow/124308677.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/un-nuclear-disarmament-meet-india-reaffirms-no-first-use-policy-urges-credible-minimum-deterrence/articleshow/124308677.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-10-04T19:28:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI News Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124308717,imgsize-695042.cms"/></item><item><title>'Deeply concerned': Sikh groups object to Pete Hegseth’s 'no-beard' rule; says i